---
import { external } from '../lib/external';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import IntroActions from '../components/IntroActions.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Support us"
  description="Support independent research on safe superintelligence. What your support enables at RESI and how to contribute."
>
  <Section id="case" class="landing">
    <h1 class="page-title">Help us build the foundations for superintelligence that is safe by design</h1>
    <p>
      RESI is an independent nonprofit research institute committed to fundamental research,
      with the focus and flexibility to respond quickly as AI develops.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our greatest need is support for people. Donations will enable us to bring in more
      researchers, especially postdocs and junior researchers, and further accelerate our research
      using AI.
    </p>
    <IntroActions
      items={[
        { label: 'Announcements', href: '/news' },
        { label: 'Meet the team', href: '/people' },
        { label: 'Explore our research program', href: '/research' },
      ]}
    />
  </Section>

  <Section id="give" divider>
    <h2 class="section-title">How to contribute</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>To discuss support and the research it would enable, contact{' '}
      <a href="mailto:funding@resi.org">funding@resi.org</a>.</strong> We also welcome compute credits,
      infrastructure support, and donated professional expertise, including specialists working
      alongside our team.
    </p>
    <p class="actions support-donate">
      <a
        class="button donate-button"
        href="https://www.every.org/resi"
        {...external('https://www.every.org/resi')}
      >
        Donate online
      </a>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="why-now" divider>
    <h2 class="section-title">Why support matters now</h2>
    <p>
      There is a limited window in which the fundamental architecture and norms surrounding
      advanced AI are still being determined.
    </p>
    <p>
      As AI systems become deeply embedded in science, medicine, finance, and everyday life,
      retrofitting safety mechanisms will become harder. It may also become harder to establish
      effective legal and institutional safeguards once these systems and the economic
      dependencies around them are entrenched.
    </p>
    <p>
      RESI is developing the intellectual foundations for trustworthy AI. The best time to do
      this work is now, while these systems are being built.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="enables" divider>
    <h2 class="section-title">What your support enables</h2>

    <div class="support-cards">
      <article class="support-card" aria-labelledby="talent">
    <h3 id="talent">Careers in independent AI safety research</h3>
    <p>
      Support gives postdocs and junior researchers time to pursue foundational questions
      alongside the{' '}
      <a href="/people">RESI team</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      We aim to sustain research careers with intellectual freedom and adequate compensation.
    </p>
      </article>
      <article class="support-card" aria-labelledby="compute">
    <h3 id="compute">Compute and tools to develop and test ideas</h3>
    <p>
      Compute and research infrastructure support implementations, proofs of concept, and
      AI-assisted research.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reliable access to compute lets researchers plan and run experiments when they need to.
    </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="why-resi" divider>
    <h2 class="section-title">Why RESI</h2>
    <p>
      Being an independent nonprofit allows us to ask the questions of what is truly required for
      increasingly powerful AI to remain trustworthy, controllable, and beneficial without our work
      being influenced by financial targets or business goals.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <a href="/research#concentration">working groups</a> and <a href="/seminars">seminars</a>{' '}
      bring together researchers across disciplines and career stages.
      This allows for knowledge transfer between senior and junior researchers. And it promotes
      the exchange of ideas, the formation of new concepts, and healthy debate between different
      subject matter experts. RESI focuses on bringing senior experts into superintelligence safety,
      as our work is built on their research and the knowledge they’ve gained throughout their careers.
    </p>
    <p class="page-foot">
      <a href="/research#areas">Explore our research areas</a> or{' '}
      <a href="/research#evidence">read foundational research by our team</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .actions.support-donate {
    margin-top: 27px;
  }
  .button.donate-button {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 10%, var(--paper));
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .button.donate-button:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, var(--paper));
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }

  .support-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .support-card {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 21px;
    border: 0.75px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 2.25px;
  }
  .support-card h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .support-card > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 570px) {
    .support-cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .support-card {
      padding: 16.5px;
    }
  }
</style>
